{"id": "EUVD-2026-104684", "enisaUuid": "158ecf27-20d7-31e0-ad5e-13c9516ca4d4", "description": "OpenSRE through 0.1.2026.10.19 contains an approval gate bypass vulnerability that allows attackers to execute shell_run commands without confirmation because the headless presenter's execution_allowed() always returns True. Attackers can inject instructions into alerts or Slack messages triaged by the agent to run commands on the host and exfiltrate LLM, Slack and cloud credentials.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T00:46:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T21:10:29", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://www.lasso.security/vulnerability-database/cve-2026-109444", "https://github.com/Tracer-Cloud/opensre/blob/8eba8c9301fa954d9eecb1693b7e2021215ec2ec/tools/interactive_shell/subprocess_presenter.py#L41", "https://github.com/Tracer-Cloud/opensre/blob/8eba8c9301fa954d9eecb1693b7e2021215ec2ec/gateway/transports/slack/processing/dispatcher.py#L276", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/opensre-through-0.1.2026.10.19-approval-gate-bypass-via-shell-run-prompt-injection"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fqh3-76w5-5vvf", "CVE-2026-109444"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "707a7178-e5ac-3e4c-9a32-254312779f87", "product": {"name": "opensre", "vendor": {"name": "Tracer-Cloud"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.1.2026.10.19"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0c453652-2e7e-3ab5-b32e-585bf73bb95d", "vendor": {"name": "Tracer-Cloud"}}], "isExploited": false}